# What must never reach an image layer.
#
# The backend and frontend images build from the REPOSITORY ROOT, because they
# copy backend/ and frontend/ respectively. That makes this file load-bearing in
# a way the per-service ones are not: without it, COPY backend/ ./ would bake
# backend/.env — the Atlas URI and the JWT secret — into a layer that stays
# readable by anyone who can pull or export the image. Deleting the file in a
# later layer would not help; layers keep their history.
#
# Secrets are handed over at RUN time with env_file instead, which keeps them
# out of the image entirely.
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.sample

# Built by npm ci inside the image; copying the host's would also drag in
# binaries compiled for the wrong architecture.
**/node_modules

# Build output, rebuilt inside the image.
frontend/dist

# Content, not engine. 4.6 GB that belongs on a mounted volume, and test data
# in an image would hand the hidden cases to anyone who pulls it.
compiler/testdata
compiler/problems
deploy/testdata
cses_problems

# Source material and notes, not code.
csnotes
*.md
!README.md

.git
.gitignore
.DS_Store
*.log
*.bak
